# Vetro "Go" profile, boot-time part (ADR 0037): on the regular image,
# androidboot.vetro.profile=go (from the host's bootloader parameters) turns
# on Android Go's low-RAM defaults before zygote starts. The values are those
# of build/make/target/board/go_defaults_common.prop and
# go_defaults_common.mk. ro.* properties can be set here only because the
# regular image does not define them; the vetro_arm64_go product defines them
# at build time instead (and removes apps, which a boot switch cannot do).

on early-init && property:ro.boot.vetro.profile=go
    setprop ro.config.low_ram true
    setprop ro.lmk.critical_upgrade true
    setprop ro.lmk.upgrade_pressure 40
    setprop ro.lmk.downgrade_pressure 60
    setprop ro.lmk.kill_heaviest_task false
    setprop dalvik.vm.heapgrowthlimit 128m
    setprop dalvik.vm.heapsize 256m
    setprop pm.dexopt.downgrade_after_inactive_days 10
    setprop ro.vetro.profile go
    write /dev/kmsg "VETRO: low-RAM (go) profile"

# microG's battery-saving exemption (sysconfig-vetro-microg.xml) is dropped
# by the vetro_arm64_go product only: init cannot run `cmd deviceidle` or
# `cmd appops` (no SELinux domain transition from init to a shell command,
# and a vendor domain may not call the platform's services), so the boot
# switch cannot restrict microG.
